# Literal data for restriction normalization and separation

The alternative list consists of the identity, ten proposed radical generators,
and 45 proposed radical-square basis matrices. These definitions assert no
spanning, independence, multiplication, or normalization theorem. In particular,
this list must be compared with `Coordinates.algebraBasis` before using it to
normalize a member of the published `concreteAlgebra`.

The test form and top operator are the literal witnesses in
`Scratch/J4FleetGuidance/SeedCentralizer/kernel-restriction.json`, generated by
`kernel_restriction.py` from the ATLAS data documented in `Janko4.Model.Data`.
Bit `56*i+j` encodes entry `(i,j)`. The source README at
`MathieuSeedCentralizer/KernelBound/source/README.md` describes the argument.

Witness SHA256: 91add245bf0d4fc3c80b64f1fd1be13d27ba2dae78d88f6abfca194eddd4ee2c.
-/

